WEBVTT

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:04.590
Would you send a survey without checking
how people understand the questions?

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.750
Think of it like a dress rehearsal.

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:10.770
You need to hear the lines clearly and
make sure the whole show runs.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.950
Start with a question pretest.

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.590
Imagine a school asking whether notices
are clear and timely.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.650
A parent may understand the notice
perfectly and still get it too late.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.890
Ask what the question meant to them.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.150
Then split it into two questions so each
answer tells you what to fix.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:30.010
Next, pilot the whole survey.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.710
Send the invitation to a small group from
the intended audience.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.210
Open it on a phone.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.650
Choose “I did not receive a notice” and
check that it skips the clarity question.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:43.870
Then open the results file and make sure
the skipped answer is blank.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:47.310
Fix the critical issues and run those
paths again.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.690
Planning a survey for a real decision?

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:52.925
